commit 02705fa0ed819bfd7d199dca88977015d3c75356
Author: Can Basaran <basaran.can@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 12:46:18 2026 +0100

    on-chain.sh: the batch cap kept per request by the runner's run guard (Zeki #10062); overshoot reservation dropped
    
    - Writes the batch guard once (late-smallchat smallchat.py guard: every paid opponent metered at its list price, one ledger, cap BATCH_CAP_USD) into BATCH_GUARD_DIR (default workspace/late-smallchat/batch-guard-<UTC>; an earlier batch's directory continues its ledger), checks its cap, creates the ledger (runner guard-ledger; refused while latched) and passes it to start.sh as GUARD_FILE (admission and league --guard).
    - ENTRY_CAP_USD + OVERSHOOT_USD reservation removed: the runner refuses any request whose worst case would pass the cap. Second line kept, read-only: before each entry the latch must be absent and billed < BATCH_CAP_USD; billed now reads the seat from turns.player (turns.side holds black/white, so CASE t.side WHEN 1 never matched and only player2's turns were counted) and books Fastino GLiDE (no cost recorded) at its $0.15/M list price.
    - start.sh's per-entry 60-s check gets ENTRY_CAP_USD (default: the batch cap). The chain stops when start.sh ends before its league runs (guard, admission or a check refused) and after an entry whose stage latched the guard.
    - CHAIN_TREE / CHAIN_BIN override the runner tree and binary (default the live late-smallchat-on worktree and its target): both must carry the guard (late-smallchat-on-wip d5d0b8d), else the chain stops before any entry.

diff --git a/workspace/on-chain.sh b/workspace/on-chain.sh
